# PROVISIONAL: measured pre-SSSR-fix. find_sssr is itself non-deterministic
# and non-minimal for ~50% of sampled molecules (single spanning-tree
# fundamental-cycle basis, zero candidate redundancy -- see project plan).
# Expect this list and its root-cause attribution to change once ring
# perception is fixed.
#
# Molecules confirmed (via atom-map-number alignment, not substructure
# matching) to give a different chematic aromaticity result depending on
# which valid Kekulized SMILES traversal is used to represent them.
# Root cause: NOT Pass 1/Pass 2 (verified order-invariant by construction --
# see plan) but `find_sssr` itself, which can return a non-minimal ring
# (e.g. a 10-membered ring in place of two 6-membered ones) depending on
# traversal order, feeding a wrong ring into otherwise order-invariant
# Huckel evaluation. See project plan for the ring-perception fix.
#
# 7 of these were already known-broken (appear in the 32-regression or
# 110-residual sets even with RDKit's canonical Kekulized form). 3 are new:
# they PASS with RDKit's canonical form specifically but fail with at least
# one other valid ordering (marked NEW below).
C1=C(c2ccccc2)N2CCCN=C2c2ccccc21
CN1N=C2C3=CC=CC=C3SC3=C2C1=CC=C3
O=C(O)Cn1c(=O)nc2n(-c3cc(C(F)(F)F)cc(C(F)(F)F)c3)c3ccccc3nc-2c1=O  # NEW
CCN(CC)CCn1nc2c3c(c(NCCNCCO)ccc31)Sc1c(OC)ccc(OC)c1-2
O=C(Nc1ccncc1)c1cccc2nc3c(N4CCN(CCc5ccc(F)c(F)c5)CC4)[nH]cnc-3c12
COc1cc(C(=O)N[C@@H]2C(=O)N[C@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N3CCC[C@@H]3C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)O[C@@H]2C)c2nc3c(C(=O)N[C@H]4C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N5CCC[C@H]5C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N(C)[C@H](C(C)C)C(=O)O[C@H]4C)c(N)c(=O)c(C)c-3oc2c1C  # NEW
CC(=O)N1c2ncccc2C(=O)N(C)c2cccnc21
Cn1c(=O)nc2n(-c3ccccc3)c3ccccc3nc-2c1=O  # NEW
